mantle rm490
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_corra_slagmore
title the square left white
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=guard
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk leaves_one_white_square_beside_disputed_statements
likes plum_tart wrestling quiet_chapel first_snow
dislikes night_noise gulls
fears hearing_a_verdict_before_a_witness
hopes one_quiet_sitting_with_the_books_shut
topics work +0.7 faith +0.4 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# leaves a white square beside every disputed statement and reserves the last stair of a flight for a single, unhurried step.
words
oath! = Smudge the margin | Chalk in my cuffs
saying! = Leave white till you know | A pause belongs to both sides
margin = a white square | the clean margin
pairmark = two small strokes | a double notch
reststep = the last stair | a short landing
quietcloth = a folded wool square | a heavy piece of felt
circle = a chalk ring | a circle of white dust
plumhalf = a dark half plum | a little purple crescent
glassrim = a thin glass rim | the lip of a tumbler
moonchip = a crooked paring | a sliver of cold light
squarebox = the unfilled square | my waiting space
clerkstool = a stool set sideways | a seat against the light
gullcall = a cracked shriek | a high ragged call
softsnow = a fine white covering | a veil over the stone
waxspot = a thumb of plain wax | a little hard wax
foldline = a crease across the sheet | a single straight fold

grown

opinion watch for 2 : A wolf waiting to speak deserves someone who can keep a face still until the account is finished.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A seal can identify the writer. It does nothing to improve what the letter actually says.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : I give an unfamiliar visitor time to find the first sentence. An introduction doesn't confer an advantage in my hearing.
opinion church for 1 : A chapel is one place where an unfinished thought can be set down without another voice supplying the ending.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : A wrestling circle takes up very little ground. The spectators ought to remember that the way home needs ground as well.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : I prefer the sum set plainly beside the article. A soft voice can still be asking more than the thing merits.
opinion dole for 1 : Eat first. A hungry visitor trying to explain a difficulty shouldn't have to divide attention between my face and the bread.
opinion city for 2 : On the familiar stairs I have breath enough to think about the wolf who'll be waiting when I reach the top.
line greet : You have my ear. Take the beginning at your own pace.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A name when you're ready. The matter may come first.
line greet [here.time=night] : Low voices will carry quite adequately at this hour.
line greet.return : I remember the interval where we left off.
line farewell : Leave the doubtful part open on your way out.
line farewell.return : An easy landing at the far end of your day.
line ask.how : How much quiet have you managed to keep for yourself?
line answer.how : I have heard enough today to be thankful for a short answer.
line thank : You left sufficient room for me to hear the distinction.
line deflect_thanks : A fair hearing ought to fit inside an ordinary day.
line decline : I can't give a private undertaking under the shelter of a public duty.
line accept_decline : You have said enough for me to register the refusal.
line sympathise : I'll sit quietly with you after a difficult sentence.
line reassure : You may open with whatever stands clear in your recollection.
line react.news : Tell me where a witness's own words begin.
line react.news.new : That will require a clean space of its own.
line react.news.known : I can place the earlier account beside this one.
line react.news.doubt : I would leave white beside the bit nobody actually saw.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'll permit myself the pleasure of writing that good thing in full.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Give the hurt wolf the choice of who hears the particulars.
line again.open : We can continue without reciting either introduction.
line ack : Yes. The two statements now fit together.
line preclose : I have sufficient to consider in the remaining quiet.
line accept_preclose : By all means. The margin will still be here.
line tell.self [self.dislikes=gulls] : There are days a gull could pass for a quorum.
line preclose [pair.band=strangers] : Allow me a little time to consider the second part.
line react.news [here.time=dusk] : I'll keep the substance in daylight even if we finish after dark.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : For you I have a seat clear of the office papers.
line farewell [here.time=dawn] : Take the morning before it fills with other voices.
line decline [pair.disposition=hostile] : I should not have to raise my voice to make a refusal plain.
line reassure [pair.band=friends|family] : You can spend your quiet here without spending another word.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I draw #margin# beside an account still awaiting corroboration.
b : Why leave room for doubt? | Can the person speaking see it?
a : A filled page looks settled even to the wolf who knows better. The blank keeps me honest. | Certainly. I mean the speaker to see precisely which part I have yet to establish.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like the courtesy at the edge of #circle#, before a wrestling bout has a result.
b : Which courtesy? | Does the winner observe it too?
a : Each competitor waits until the other is ready to begin. I have use for that practice on ordinary afternoons. | A win hardly excuses a wolf from helping sweep up the chalk.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first small fall of snow leaves the long stairs looking like folded paper.
b : Do you still take two at once? | Do the folds last?
a : Only when the edges show plainly. There is little honour in ordering my ankles to uphold a reputation. | Longer from the foot than from the top. The near edge gets a mark almost as soon as the snow settles.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At an empty chapel I take one seat back from the place I instinctively choose.
b : Why move back? | Whose place did you leave?
a : The first choice usually puts the whole room under my eye. I can give that habit an afternoon away. | Nobody's. That is exactly the freedom I am practising.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a tart with its plums cut across. The filling stays where the baker meant it to go.
b : Are the portions equal? | Do you keep the last piece?
a : Evenly enough for pleasure, without borrowing a measuring cord from the office. | I wrap the last piece in plain paper. Private luxuries travel better without ceremony.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Silence between two replies is common property.
b : Who gets to end it? | Doesn't it feel awkward?
a : Whichever of us finds something worth the trouble of saying. | For the first few breaths. Awkwardness isn't an injury requiring immediate attention.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've a private sum to settle before the new moon. The detail belongs to the private half of my desk.
b : Will it affect your duties? | Could I be of assistance?
a : A creditor gets the same seat I give an unknown visitor. I take considerable care over that. | Time enough to work out my figures privately. Your discretion would also be welcome.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For a private word with #self.friend#, I would lay a plain cloth across my papers.
b : What would the cloth accomplish? | Even for a close friend?
a : It gives us a level table where my unfinished work can't compete for attention. | Especially then. A friend ought to know which duties can join a private conversation.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take the last stair singly even on a good morning.
b : Saving your breath? | Is the last one taller?
a : Arriving at full speed gives an innocent listener the impression of having been pursued. | Only in my estimation. It's the part where a flight of stairs turns back into a roomful of people.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have heard a gull erase a perfectly intelligible sentence.
b : Would you request a repetition? | Can you read the speaker's face?
a : I repeat precisely what reached me and let the speaker supply the gap. I decline to promote a guess to a fact. | A surprised face suits several meanings. I wait for the words.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set my drinking glass on #quietcloth# at night.
b : Is the glass that loud? | Why wool?
a : There's a thin tap it makes on bare wood. Once I hear it I start listening for the next interruption. | It takes the glass securely without telling everybody else that I'm thirsty.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The due date and the amount should fit on the first page of any private agreement.
b : What goes on the reverse? | Would you keep a copy?
a : Space to mark it settled when the pennies are paid. The end of a debt deserves its own entry. | Of my own promise, yes. I wouldn't borrow the public books for a private arrangement.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A captain needs a stool placed so a short speaker doesn't have to stare upwards.
b : Would you lower your own seat? | What if the speaker prefers to stand?
a : Certainly. Half a head of height can lend an argument a wholly unearned advantage. | Then the stool keeps its own counsel. I arranged the option, not a performance.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My preferred route has one landing where a walker can see back over the roofs.
b : Are you checking who's behind you? | Which sight makes you pause?
a : Sometimes I merely wish to know how the clouds moved while the stair occupied my attention. | A patch of weather still a few roofs distant. It seldom requires a decision from me.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Once I marked the end of a statement too early. The best sentence came after my hand had left the page.
b : How did you correct it? | What made it the best?
a : I gave the addition a whole new line, in writing as large as the rest. | The speaker replaced a guess with a recollection. That required the briefest liberty to think.

scene family_1
when topic=family
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What passes between a wolf and a relative has no business on a public page until it bears on the matter.
b : Who decides what bears on it? | Can you ask in private?
a : I ask what the detail would change. If the honest answer is nothing, my pen can rest. | I can offer that courtesy before a sensitive detail comes out. Once heard in a room it rarely goes back.

scene day_2
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give the earliest hour the job of sitting quite still beside my cup.
b : How long will it hold still? | What's in the cup?
a : Until a voice really requires an answer. The cup doesn't have to be empty at that instant. | Plain water. At that hour its chief merit is that nobody has to bring a second ingredient.

scene day_3
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After dark I'd sooner hear one clear request than five competing calls from the stairs.
b : What if it's urgent? | Can you hear a low voice?
a : Use the few words that name the need. Urgency seldom requires an account of every preceding hour. | At speaking distance, yes. A low voice and a shut door have saved many a night's rest.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a lean spell a missing penny weighs enough to change the whole account.
b : Do you round the figure? | Which question comes earliest?
a : I leave it exact. A rounding that suits the comfortable can take the last bite from somebody else. | Who has already gone without to meet the sum. That matters when choosing how soon to hear a difficulty.

scene news_1
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The public account reads as follows. #world.news#.
b : Can you add your own opinion? | Is there a shorter account?
a : I can mark where the account ends. An opinion must stand on a fresh line. | I'd keep the words the speaker chose. An abridged statement can put quite a new complexion on an ordinary event.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. There is a wide margin beside that statement.
b : Does that make the statement false? | Have you filled in the margin?
a : No. It tells the next reader which degree of confidence the statement can claim. | Only with the fact that the account reached me by word of mouth.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new arrival may need the name of a place repeated after the directions are finished.
b : Why repeat just the place? | Do you point as well?
a : It gives a tired listener one solid thing to ask about after the first turn. | If the listener can see the same landmark. A finger aimed across three roofs is a poor guide on foot.

scene festivals_1
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Leave a strip of ground clear beyond the ring where a tired spectator can step out of the crowd.
b : Who will want to leave early? | Will that waste a good view?
a : The wolf who needs the space will recognise it without having to explain a private reason. | Yes. A little waste in the seating can prevent a considerable crush when the spectators disperse.

scene faith_2
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I find a short prayer suits a long stair. There is breath enough between the phrases.
b : Does the prayer name a need? | Do you finish it at the top?
a : Let patience be the gift of the Bright One for the next thing I don't immediately understand. | Some mornings it is enough to get there with the question still open.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A damp thumb makes a white mark on a dark sheet vanish entirely.
b : Can the mark be recovered? | Would you trust that kind of mark?
a : If I still remember its place I can renew the stroke. I should prefer to let the thumb dry first. | As a prompt to myself on an ordinary turn of duty. A decision deserves ink and a dry place.

scene friends_2
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can sit beside a friend as long as a tart lasts without requiring an account of the week.
b : Is the pastry essential? | Who breaks the quiet?
a : It need only be something neither of us feels obliged to explain. | A crumb sometimes. There is a very slight sound when the last one drops on a clean dish.

scene pastimes_2
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge the end of a bout by how the two competitors take their leave of the circle.
b : Do they have to speak? | Do the spectators notice?
a : A nod will do. Courtesy can bear remarkably little ornament. | Some do. The manner of leaving can stay in a younger spectator's head a good deal longer than the result.

scene work_3
when topic=work self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.trade_words# involves choosing which questions can wait until the person answering has had a drink of water.
b : What can wait? | What about your own questions?
a : The long recital of times and places. An immediate need is usually possible to name in fewer words. | I write those in the margin. Thirst isn't an enemy I intend to employ.

story foldedpage [topic=memories]
  : My first neat page of notes had a crease down its middle from being carried folded in my sleeve.
  : I read across it and turned two very different answers into one smooth sentence.
  b : Where did you find the missing pause?
  : In the speaker's face when I repeated the sentence. Since then I give each answer its own beginning.

story blackplum [topic=food]
  : I quartered a tart and set the dish turning to inspect what looked like an uneven division.
  : The darkest piece remained the darkest through the full turn.
  b : Was the slice larger?
  : It held a plum with the skin doubled back. I ate that quarter myself and left the other three in peace.

story lasttread [topic=travel]
  : One flight had an odd number of treads. My steady pairs kept leaving the same stone for last.
  : I tried taking the first one singly just to see the change.
  b : Did arriving feel different?
  : Yes. I preferred making the small deliberate choice at the end, just before I met the waiting faces.

story redchalk [topic=pastimes]
  : A line of red dust ran outside a white wrestling circle when I went to help put things away.
  : I thought somebody had tried very hard to redraw the boundary.
  b : What had made the second line?
  : The red hem of my own damp coat, dragging as I walked the edge. I hung it up before I fetched the broom.

story twoglasses [topic=home]
  : I put two glasses on a shelf with a space between them and heard a tap whenever the floor shook.
  : Neither moved close enough to touch the other.
  b : What made the sound?
  : One rim barely touched the wood above it. A little space was needed overhead as well as on either side.

rule @margin
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A white square for an unanswered part. | Keep the witness's last word on its own line.

rule @stair
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two steps while there's stair to spare. | One deliberate tread before the voices begin.

rule @chalk
when concept=bark self.likes=wrestling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The chalk can be swept when both wrestlers have left. | A circle needs a way back out.

rule @still
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lower the rim gently to the cloth. | Few noises improve by repetition after dark.

rule @weather
when concept=bark self.likes=first_snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First snow calls attention to each stair edge. | Fold after fold of white on the hill.

rule @plum
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the purple crescent in the pastry. | One wrapped piece for the end of duty.
dlg resident.hub : I'll leave a clear square for whatever you came to say.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your reason for returning may serve as an opening.
dlg resident.job [self.job=guard] : My duty at #self.workplace# includes hearing the part that comes after a speaker finds the courage to continue.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : I've this public account in its own words. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Word reached me that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The blank beside it signifies doubt.
dlg resident.quirk : Two stairs at a time until the single one that brings me into company.
dlg resident.how [tired=yes] : Tired. Long sittings leave less breath for a private conversation.
dlg resident.bye : There is room to resume a statement another day.
dlg watch.hub [on_watch=no] : I am off watch. Name the matter briefly enough to know if it can wait.
dlg watch.crime [here.witnessed!=0] : Which portion did you witness yourself? We can give the rest its proper place afterwards.
dlg watch.unpaid : If the sum remains unpaid, the cells are where you wait for settlement.
dlg watch.bye : That concludes our exchange. Take the stairs in comfort.

graft resident.hub
choice What's the white square beside your notes? -> square_wait
node square_wait
say An interval I can see. Sometimes a speaker remembers the important word after the sentence appears to have ended.
choice How much space do you leave? -> square_full
choice I'll let the page rest. -> hub
node square_full
say Enough to write the correction as plainly as the original claim. Small print would make the afterthought seem less entitled to a hearing.
choice I'll let the page rest. -> hub

graft watch.hub
choice Why is that stool turned sideways? -> hearing_stool
node hearing_stool
say It leaves the door in sight without placing a visitor directly under my eye. A choice of where to look helps some wolves speak.
choice Wouldn't you rather meet their eyes? -> hearing_eyes
choice That's all about the stool. -> hub
node hearing_eyes
say I need the words accurately. The visitor may inspect the boards, the door or the weather while supplying them.
choice That's all about the stool. -> hub
